# RoadSOS Master Development Rulebook

The canonical checklist is **`docs/DEVELOPMENT_RULEBOOK.md`** (200+ rules, 9 phases). Follow phases in the **priority order** in that file’s “Quick reference — priority order” section (Security and Planning before implementation).

## Definitions

- **`[CRITICAL]`**: Ignoring this risks failure, legal liability, or harm to life — must be verified for any touched code path in review.
- Use tags `[COLLAB]`, `[INDIA]`, `[AI/ML]`, `[SECURITY]` as filters when scoping work and reviews.

## Agent / review behavior

1. Before new features: confirm **Phase 1** (unconscious-user test, MVP SOS, failure modes, Real vs Simulated) and **Phase 5** when data or auth is involved.
2. On every PR: for each file changed, skim **all `[CRITICAL]` items** that apply to that area (dispatch, orchestrator, AI triage, BLE, maps, secrets).
3. Never ship **Simulated** behavior as **Real**; document honest feature status (README / internal table per rulebook Phase 8).
4. Prefer small, reviewable PRs and Conventional Commits per Phase 8; two reviewers for `EmergencyOrchestrator` changes.

When in doubt, open the `docs/` checklist and quote the relevant phase and tag in the PR or commit message context.
